version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
url: "https://github.com/TheFinalDreamer/scAgent-DPM"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheFinalDreamer/scAgent-DPM"
abstract: >-
  scAgent-DPM is a rule-based, domain-aware workflow for reproducible single-cell
  perturbation analysis. It orchestrates input validation and schema harmonization,
  matrix-state-aware preprocessing, metric-aware adaptive quality control,
  per-cell-type differential expression with Wilcoxon and Benjamini-Hochberg
  correction, structured pathway enrichment with explicit status tracking, and a
  component-aware Drug Perturbation Response Score (DPRS) that records unavailable
  components explicitly rather than imputing them. The workflow is an orchestration
  layer, not a predictive perturbation-response model, and contains no language model.
  This release is a curated public snapshot of the canonical source and configurations
  used for the associated CMPB manuscript (CMPB-D-26-07112); it is not the original
  experimental commit, as the experimental working tree was not under version control.
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - perturbation analysis
  - workflow reproducibility
  - pathway enrichment
  - differential expression
  - quality control
  - bioinformatics
license: MIT
type: software
